   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region; the cis cyclohexane assignment is the least certain part.\n\n**Regions, left to right**\n- **Phenol:** a 2-hydroxyphenyl ring is attached to the pyridazine.\n- **Pyridazine:** the ring reads N=N\u2013C(NH2)=C(pyrazolyl)\u2013CH=C(aryl). The amino group sits next to a ring nitrogen, and the pyrazole is on the adjacent carbon.\n- **Pyrazole:** it is linked through C4 to the pyridazine and through N1 to the piperidine C4. This gives `c1cnn(c1)` in the SMILES.\n- **Piperidine:** it is substituted at C4 by the pyrazole N and at N1 by the cyclohexane.\n- **Cyclohexane:** it carries the piperidine N on one carbon and a CH2\u2013NH group on the carbon opposite (1,4). Both of these bonds are drawn as hashes.\n- **Right-hand end:** the NH is bonded to C5 of an isoindoline-1,3-dione. The imide N bears a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group, which has no stereo marking and so gets none.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** with both hashed bonds pointing the same way on the ring, the 1,4-substituents are cis. For the SMILES pattern `N[C@H]1CC[C@@H](C...)CC1`, working through the geometry gives `@,@@` as cis, so I used that.\n\nSMILES: Nc1nnc(-c2ccccc2O)cc1-c1cnn(c1)C1CCN(CC1)[C@H]1CC[C@@H](CNc2ccc3C(=O)N(C4CCC(=O)NC4=O)C(=O)c3c2)CC1"
